  "studentQuestionsAI": {
    "headline": "1.3 million visits this fall; course lookups dominate, career and research content trails far behind.",
    "summary": "Between August 19 and November 17, 2026, the site drew 1,287,771 visits, nearly three-quarters of them first-time visitors. On-site searches show students are mostly hunting for specific courses, while careers, internships, and research together account for just over 2 percent of search activity?suggesting those pages exist but are not yet pulling people in.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "insight": "Careers and internships made up only 1.4 percent of on-site searches, which likely reflects thin content rather than low student interest?departments supplying graduate outcome data would give these pages something worth searching for."
      },
      {
        "n": 2,
        "insight": "Majors, minors, and programs accounted for 5.3 percent of on-site searches, with public health, neuroscience, and zoology among the top terms, pointing to programs where stronger program descriptions could capture more of that interest."
      },
      {
        "n": 3,
        "insight": "Advising and course permissions drew 4.5 percent of on-site searches, with 'advising,' 'readmission,' and 'advisor' all appearing, suggesting students are actively looking for advisor contact information and next-step guidance."
      },
      {
        "n": 4,
        "insight": "Research represented only 0.8 percent of on-site searches, though specific terms like 'REU,' 'bridges lab,' and 'psychology research' show that students who do search know what they want?more department-level lab and opportunity listings could surface those pages earlier."
      },
      {
        "n": 5,
        "insight": "Graduate programs did not appear as a distinct search cluster in this period, making it difficult to gauge demand; without funding details, application deadlines, and placement records from departments, the web team has little to build those pages around."
      }
    ],
